1
00:00:12,112 --> 00:00:13,213
Dr. Kaji!

2
00:00:16,116 --> 00:00:17,817
Thank you very much.

3
00:00:18,385 --> 00:00:19,619
Please be at ease.

4
00:00:19,819 --> 00:00:22,389
Your kidney cancer was cleanly removed.

5
00:00:23,423 --> 00:00:26,393
Recovery after laparoscopic surgery
is quick,

6
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:27,927
so you can walk out in three days.

7
00:00:28,395 --> 00:00:31,898
Other hospitals told us
laparoscopic surgery would be tough.

8
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:35,101
Father, we're really lucky, right?

9
00:00:35,969 --> 00:00:38,505
Dr. Kaji, I'm alive thanks to you.

10
00:00:38,571 --> 00:00:40,573
- Thank you very much.
- Thank you very much!

11
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:44,310
Not at all, I just did my job as a surg--

12
00:00:44,411 --> 00:00:45,512
Cut, cut!

13
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:48,615
Something strange came in to the picture!

14
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:52,318
Get out of the way!

15
00:00:53,019 --> 00:00:55,422
Sorry, could you do it one more time?

16
00:00:55,488 --> 00:00:58,158
From "I'm alive thanks to you."

17
00:01:00,193 --> 00:01:02,295
What a nuisance for the patients.

18
00:01:02,362 --> 00:01:03,363
MICHIKO DAIMON
FREELANCE SURGEON

19
00:01:03,430 --> 00:01:04,497
Enough. I'm out of time.

20
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:05,398
#2 SURGERY - TEACHER
HIDEKI KAJI

21
00:01:06,099 --> 00:01:08,001
Just once more!
We need you to do it once more!

22
00:01:08,134 --> 00:01:09,135
MARIKO YOSHINAGA
NEWSCASTER

23
00:01:09,602 --> 00:01:10,437
Please!

24
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:14,808
It can't be helped.
Let's go from that part.

25
00:01:15,608 --> 00:01:18,344
It's better if you...
put more feeling into it.

26
00:01:18,478 --> 00:01:19,579
- Feeling.
- Yes.

27
00:01:22,182 --> 00:01:26,286
Other hospitals told us
laparoscopic surgery would be tough!

28
00:01:26,352 --> 00:01:29,956
<i>Dr. Kaji, I'm alive thanks to you!</i>

29
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:31,091
<i>Thank you very much!</i>

30
00:01:31,157 --> 00:01:33,693
<i>Not at all,</i>
<i>I just did my job as a surgeon.</i>

31
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,762
LAPAROSCOPIC MAGICIAN
DR. HIDEKI KAJI

32
00:01:36,796 --> 00:01:38,465
He's so cool!

33
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:40,967
Kaji looks even better than usual today.

34
00:01:41,234 --> 00:01:42,235
HIROMI JONOUCHI
ANESTHESIOLOGIST

35
00:01:42,302 --> 00:01:43,336
He even left his gown unbuttoned.

36
00:01:48,541 --> 00:01:50,276
TRUE RECORD
THE SUPER DOCTOR

37
00:01:50,343 --> 00:01:52,912
LAPAROSCOPIC MAGICIAN
DR.<i></i>HIDEKI KAJI

38
00:01:53,379 --> 00:01:56,683
Chief, this will bring in
more outpatients!

39
00:01:57,250 --> 00:02:01,254
Hospital stays are shorter
with laparoscopic surgery,

40
00:02:01,721 --> 00:02:04,224
which improves the turnover rate,
meaning it's good for business.

41
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:05,225
KANEKO TERAYAMA
MANAGER

42
00:02:05,291 --> 00:02:06,426
Certainly.

43
00:02:06,893 --> 00:02:08,862
RYUNOSUKE BUSUJIMA
HOSPITAL CHIEF

44
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:16,536
ATSUSHI YOTSUYA
FUND MANAGER

45
00:02:24,978 --> 00:02:26,012
WORLD TRADE FX

46
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:35,288
- We got the financing for 300 million yen.
- Oh.

47
00:02:39,025 --> 00:02:41,127
<i>Thanks to you, I'm alive!</i>

48
00:02:41,594 --> 00:02:43,696
<i>Thank you very much!</i>

49
00:02:44,197 --> 00:02:47,133
<i>Recovery after laparoscopic surgery</i>
<i>is quick,</i>

50
00:02:47,534 --> 00:02:48,902
<i>so you can walk out in three days.</i>

51
00:02:48,968 --> 00:02:51,471
<i>- Thank you very much!</i>
<i>- Thank you very much!</i>

52
00:02:55,275 --> 00:02:57,610
TRUE RECORD SUPER DOCTOR
LAPAROSCOPIC MAGICIAN DR. HIDEKI KAJI

53
00:02:58,478 --> 00:03:00,046
Laparoscopic magician...

54
00:03:15,228 --> 00:03:17,931
<i>Even though there are</i>
<i>wonderful doctors like Dr. Kaji,</i>

55
00:03:17,997 --> 00:03:19,966
<i>the surgeon shortage</i>
<i>is a hot topic these days.</i>

56
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:23,303
<i>What does super doctor, Dr. Kaji,</i>
<i>think about this issue?</i>

57
00:03:23,369 --> 00:03:25,738
<i>Surgeons have a tough job, with</i>
<i>a high chance of malpractice lawsuits.</i>

58
00:03:25,805 --> 00:03:26,806
TRUE RECORD! SPECIAL INTERVIEW
MEDICINE FOR DR. KAJI

59
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:28,374
<i>It's certainly not</i>
<i>an ideal work environment.</i>

60
00:03:28,808 --> 00:03:33,079
<i>Perhaps that's why freelance doctors</i>
<i>have influence these days.</i>

61
00:03:33,146 --> 00:03:34,080
HIKARU MORIMOTO
#2 SURGERY - ASSISTANT

62
00:03:34,147 --> 00:03:37,150
<i>Can you possibly trust your life</i>
<i>to irresponsible people like that?</i>

63
00:03:37,717 --> 00:03:40,653
<i>Dr. Kaji, what is</i>
<i>the dignity of a doctor to you?</i>

64
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:44,958
<i>It's whether you can find meaning</i>
<i>in your life by saving patients' lives.</i>

65
00:03:46,659 --> 00:03:47,927
<i>It's not about money.</i>

66
00:03:49,062 --> 00:03:50,463
<i>It's not about money.</i>

67
00:03:51,631 --> 00:03:54,234
<i>For me, surgery is priceless life work.</i>

68
00:03:55,401 --> 00:03:56,436
All right!

69
00:04:00,673 --> 00:04:03,076
- Professor, good morning.
- Good morning.

70
00:04:03,543 --> 00:04:06,746
Kaji, exposure through the media
is fine and all...

71
00:04:07,213 --> 00:04:08,214
TAKASHI TORII
#2 SURGERY CHIEF - PROFESSOR

72
00:04:08,281 --> 00:04:10,783
...but if you don't write research papers
there's no future as a medical scientist.

73
00:04:10,850 --> 00:04:14,087
That's fine. I have no ambition at all
to become a professor.

74
00:04:14,153 --> 00:04:18,091
If it's not about power,
it's about money after all, no?

75
00:04:18,157 --> 00:04:20,893
That's right... I mean, I'm not like you!

76
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:24,631
Not at all.
I'm not as money hungry as you.

77
00:04:24,697 --> 00:04:26,866
That's why I said I'm not like you!

78
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:28,735
Dr. Kaji seems
to get mad easily these days.

79
00:04:28,801 --> 00:04:29,869
MAMORU HARA
#2 SURGERY - ASSISTANT PROFESSOR

80
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:31,738
Yeah, since Daimon came here.

81
00:04:32,972 --> 00:04:36,743
Freelancers should act like freelancers
and quickly disappear somewhere!

82
00:04:36,809 --> 00:04:37,744
Okay!

83
00:04:39,679 --> 00:04:41,981
I'm off to pancreatic cancer surgery.

84
00:04:45,084 --> 00:04:48,388
<i>I'm sure he'll continue</i>
<i>to save lives in the future, too.</i>

85
00:04:48,855 --> 00:04:50,723
<i>True Record: Super Doctor!</i>

86
00:04:51,090 --> 00:04:54,193
<i>Which wonderful doctor</i>
<i>will we get to meet next time?</i>

87
00:04:54,994 --> 00:04:58,631
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

88
00:04:59,899 --> 00:05:02,568
<i>Medicine in university hospitals</i>
<i>has weakened,</i>

89
00:05:02,769 --> 00:05:05,204
<i>and even medicine, which deals with life,</i>

90
00:05:05,271 --> 00:05:08,574
<i>has already entered the era</i>
<i>of the law of the jungle.</i>

91
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:12,578
<i>To fill this critical shortage</i>
<i>in the medical field, freelance...</i>

92
00:05:15,581 --> 00:05:18,618
- Doctor, thank you for everything!
- Take care.

93
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:24,223
<i>...in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors, have emerged.</i>

94
00:05:31,464 --> 00:05:33,966
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

95
00:05:35,301 --> 00:05:36,669
<i>Also known as...</i>

96
00:05:37,570 --> 00:05:38,805
<i>Doctor X.</i>

97
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:48,748
DOCTOR X SURGEON MICHIKO DAIMON
EPISODE 4

98
00:05:51,084 --> 00:05:53,319
Today's patient was really overweight.

99
00:05:53,953 --> 00:05:55,388
Maybe I'll skip lunch.

100
00:05:55,888 --> 00:06:00,293
When you operate through layers of fat,
don't you lose your appetite?

101
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:02,562
- Stamina Tontoro lunch special.
- What?

102
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:05,431
- Dr. Daimon, you're not affected
by that at all.

103
00:06:05,498 --> 00:06:06,699
What? Not at all.

104
00:06:06,766 --> 00:06:08,735
Here you go, Tontoro Lunch Special.

105
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:21,814
Yotsuya, what's up so suddenly?

106
00:06:21,881 --> 00:06:24,617
Hold on a sec.
The Singapore market is trading right now.

107
00:06:25,785 --> 00:06:26,886
As usual.

108
00:06:29,155 --> 00:06:30,490
EUR/USD - DONE
TRANSACTION ESTABLISHED

109
00:06:32,625 --> 00:06:35,995
It's been a while.
I saw you on TV this morning and came.

110
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:37,730
You're always busy. What's wrong?

111
00:06:38,030 --> 00:06:41,567
It's trouble. They found it
when I took the company physical.

112
00:06:41,667 --> 00:06:42,769
Stage 1 cancer.

113
00:06:43,870 --> 00:06:45,304
Really? Where?

114
00:06:45,371 --> 00:06:46,539
In the duodenum.

115
00:06:46,773 --> 00:06:48,808
I need to get back to work ASAP.

116
00:06:48,875 --> 00:06:50,343
I want to have
laparoscopic surgery immediately.

117
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:51,477
Immediately?

118
00:06:51,644 --> 00:06:53,646
Every day I'm off could mean
hundreds of millions in losses.

119
00:06:53,713 --> 00:06:55,715
Wait just a minute. I'm busy, too.

120
00:06:56,315 --> 00:06:58,651
I'm fully booked for the next month.

121
00:07:00,486 --> 00:07:02,655
I'll pay a huge tip. Please!

122
00:07:03,122 --> 00:07:04,424
I don't know.

123
00:07:04,991 --> 00:07:07,226
I have many patients waiting for me,

124
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:10,696
but I can't ignore a classmate, can I?

125
00:07:17,403 --> 00:07:19,338
Torii's #2 Surgery.

126
00:07:20,039 --> 00:07:24,043
I hear there's been a dramatic increase
of outpatients and referrals.

127
00:07:24,210 --> 00:07:25,445
Yes, thank you.

128
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:30,016
Is it thanks to that super doctor
who's on TV all the time?

129
00:07:30,082 --> 00:07:35,188
Well, Kaji is well known
for his skill in laparoscopic surgery.

130
00:07:35,755 --> 00:07:37,223
He also likes the spotlight.

131
00:07:38,224 --> 00:07:40,993
Dr. Kaji has star quality,

132
00:07:41,594 --> 00:07:44,697
but while Professor Torii is conservative,
he's also a great surgeon.

133
00:07:45,164 --> 00:07:46,599
Thank you very much.

134
00:07:47,066 --> 00:07:49,068
Ah, now that you mention it,

135
00:07:49,635 --> 00:07:51,537
I heard that you succeeded with

136
00:07:51,704 --> 00:07:55,007
a difficult surgery
on the Nikaido Publishing President.

137
00:07:55,708 --> 00:07:58,144
Why not present about it at a conference?

138
00:07:58,845 --> 00:08:01,914
No, it actually wasn't that difficult.

139
00:08:04,884 --> 00:08:07,753
How can this be!
It's spread more than expected.

140
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,455
The artery's entangled in the tumor.

141
00:08:09,522 --> 00:08:13,259
Have Daimon come
to Operation Room #1 immediately.

142
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:16,229
Move! You're in the way.

143
00:08:17,163 --> 00:08:19,031
<i>I will not fail.</i>

144
00:08:24,704 --> 00:08:28,241
As you can see, Torii is very modest.

145
00:08:29,008 --> 00:08:33,145
Actually, I was fortunate enough
to be there to observe it,

146
00:08:33,446 --> 00:08:35,448
but it really was a brilliant surgery.

147
00:08:42,121 --> 00:08:44,590
Next is your specialty: research papers.

148
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:47,927
I look forward
to the next academic conference.

149
00:09:01,274 --> 00:09:02,308
<i>Pon.</i>

150
00:09:03,643 --> 00:09:06,178
Do you know why the divorce rate
for surgeons is so high?

151
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:11,784
It's best to have affairs using duty
and emergency surgeries as excuses,

152
00:09:12,318 --> 00:09:14,487
and there are many affairs
with nurses and woman doctors.

153
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:17,456
Come to think of it,
Hideki Kaji is divorced, too.

154
00:09:17,523 --> 00:09:19,559
I saw him on TV,
but he's on a roll these days.

155
00:09:20,927 --> 00:09:22,161
<i>Pon!</i>

156
00:09:23,996 --> 00:09:26,866
Is he really a super doctor?

157
00:09:26,933 --> 00:09:29,201
No doubt he's an amazing
laparoscopic surgeon.

158
00:09:31,470 --> 00:09:34,840
He's always off doing a demonstration
operation, so I've never seen it.

159
00:09:35,274 --> 00:09:36,175
Seriously.

160
00:09:36,275 --> 00:09:40,279
Only the doctors who are cash-obsessed
go around saying pretentious things like,

161
00:09:40,446 --> 00:09:41,914
"It's not about money, but is life work."

162
00:09:42,148 --> 00:09:44,684
The other day he was at a club in Ginza,

163
00:09:45,184 --> 00:09:47,620
showing off his money
and talking big to the hostesses.

164
00:09:47,687 --> 00:09:48,921
He said stuff like,

165
00:09:48,988 --> 00:09:52,758
"In university hospital operation rooms,
there's lots of money."

166
00:09:52,825 --> 00:09:55,227
- He's that kind of guy after all.
- Right.

167
00:09:55,294 --> 00:09:58,764
Patients that need difficult surgeries
gather at university hospitals,

168
00:09:58,864 --> 00:10:00,366
and the tips are large.

169
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:01,434
AKIRA KAMBARA
DOCTOR REFERRAL AGENCY CHIEF

170
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:04,704
Michiko, if there's lots of money,
why don't you take advantage of it too?

171
00:10:04,870 --> 00:10:06,906
You haven't even paid
this month's interest.

172
00:10:06,973 --> 00:10:09,208
I know.

173
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:11,911
<i>Ron! </i>Wow!

174
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:15,815
<i>Daisangen Yakuman.</i>

175
00:10:16,849 --> 00:10:19,285
Wow!

176
00:10:20,186 --> 00:10:21,187
Wow.

177
00:10:25,491 --> 00:10:26,459
How are you feeling?

178
00:10:28,628 --> 00:10:32,164
I felt sick as soon as I checked in
and changed into pajamas.

179
00:10:32,765 --> 00:10:34,066
You sound bearish.

180
00:10:34,967 --> 00:10:37,737
Kaji... I'm sorry about that time.

181
00:10:39,605 --> 00:10:41,974
Now your divine hands are my only hope.

182
00:10:42,575 --> 00:10:43,776
I'm counting on you.

183
00:10:44,577 --> 00:10:48,314
Anyways, I'll do my best. Don't worry.

184
00:10:55,955 --> 00:10:56,789
Here.

185
00:10:59,025 --> 00:10:59,959
Cut it out.

186
00:11:00,292 --> 00:11:02,361
Shouldn't I give it to you before surgery?

187
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:04,563
I heard it's not effective after surgery.

188
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:08,200
There may be doctors like that,
but I'm different.

189
00:11:13,072 --> 00:11:15,441
All right, after a successful surgery.

190
00:11:22,148 --> 00:11:24,917
- You were classmates at Nada High School?
- Yeah.

191
00:11:25,051 --> 00:11:29,455
He's a foreign fund manager
who deals with billions of yen every day.

192
00:11:30,322 --> 00:11:32,191
- Dr. Kaji, may I ask something?
- Sure.

193
00:11:32,258 --> 00:11:34,593
He said he was sorry about that time.
What happened?

194
00:11:35,127 --> 00:11:38,931
Oh. At a class reunion a few years ago,
he insulted me.

195
00:11:39,899 --> 00:11:42,234
He said, "No matter how hard you study,

196
00:11:42,301 --> 00:11:44,203
no matter how you improve
your surgical skill,

197
00:11:44,303 --> 00:11:47,740
Kaji Hideki, your annual income
is my income in five seconds."

198
00:11:48,741 --> 00:11:50,409
What? That's unforgivable.

199
00:11:50,476 --> 00:11:54,246
But he probably realized the value
of doctors now that he's sick.

200
00:11:54,313 --> 00:11:57,783
Well, whether he lives or dies,
it's in my hands now.

201
00:11:57,850 --> 00:12:00,686
- Doctors shouldn't be about money, right?
- Right.

202
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:02,488
It's priceless life work.

203
00:12:02,788 --> 00:12:06,192
But there's lots of tip money
laying around in operation rooms, right?

204
00:12:06,258 --> 00:12:08,160
That's ri-- What are you saying?

205
00:12:08,227 --> 00:12:11,764
Don't stand behind me!
Everything about you pisses me off!

206
00:12:12,198 --> 00:12:15,634
- Dr. Kaji, calm down! Don't mind her.
- What the hell!

207
00:12:16,669 --> 00:12:17,770
Quit it!

208
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:20,873
We will start this week's
pre-operation conference.

209
00:12:20,973 --> 00:12:21,907
PRE-OPERATION CONFERENCE

210
00:12:21,974 --> 00:12:23,909
Forty-five years old, Atsushi Yotsuya.

211
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:27,880
Duodenal cancer was found
during a physical exam,

212
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:30,182
and he wants surgery as soon as possible.

213
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:36,122
Since the patient sought my help,
I will be the main surgeon.

214
00:12:36,622 --> 00:12:39,692
Kaji, I believe your schedule
is full for some time.

215
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:42,027
I've asked Hara
to take one surgery for me.

216
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:42,928
Oh, I see.

217
00:12:44,663 --> 00:12:46,565
Duodenum descending part cancer,
Stage 1...

218
00:12:46,632 --> 00:12:47,633
DUODENUM DESCENDING PART CANCER

219
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:48,868
...two centimeters in diameter.

220
00:12:49,335 --> 00:12:51,470
We will be performing
open abdominal surgery.

221
00:12:52,138 --> 00:12:53,606
What? Open?

222
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:55,808
Not a laparoscopy?

223
00:12:56,275 --> 00:12:57,610
I will continue.

224
00:12:57,676 --> 00:13:00,746
That patient said he'll lose hundreds
of millions for every day he's off,

225
00:13:00,813 --> 00:13:03,582
so he wanted a laparoscopy
to get out quickly.

226
00:13:03,649 --> 00:13:06,485
- None of your business.
- But he said that in the cafeteria, no?

227
00:13:07,419 --> 00:13:08,521
Is that so?

228
00:13:08,821 --> 00:13:12,725
Dr. Kaji, as I always say,
compliance-wise,

229
00:13:12,892 --> 00:13:15,427
we must respect the patient's wishes.

230
00:13:15,494 --> 00:13:16,695
I understand that, but--

231
00:13:16,762 --> 00:13:19,431
An open abdominal surgery
needs a longer stay,

232
00:13:19,498 --> 00:13:21,300
and the QOL might decline.

233
00:13:22,067 --> 00:13:23,269
- Demon.
- It's Daimon.

234
00:13:23,335 --> 00:13:25,404
I'm well aware of that
without you saying it.

235
00:13:25,471 --> 00:13:29,708
Chief, may I take a few minutes
to educate this know-it-all freelancer?

236
00:13:31,177 --> 00:13:33,012
- Go ahead.
- Thank you very much.

237
00:13:34,814 --> 00:13:36,882
Finding duodenum tumors is very difficult.

238
00:13:37,183 --> 00:13:39,552
It's even difficult for me,
a laparoscopic magician, to remove them.

239
00:13:39,618 --> 00:13:43,389
With early stage cancer that's entered
submucosa, risk of metastasis is small.

240
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:46,325
Therefore, in order to avoid
an excessive pancreaticduodenectomy,

241
00:13:46,392 --> 00:13:50,362
it's best to open the abdomen for partial
duodenum resection. I'm saying that!

242
00:13:51,197 --> 00:13:54,166
If finding the position is difficult,
why not do an endoscopy too?

243
00:13:54,433 --> 00:13:56,635
If used simultaneously,
you can do a laparoscopy.

244
00:13:56,702 --> 00:13:58,571
There's no way
you can use both at the same time!

245
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:00,739
Why? I can do it.

246
00:14:02,241 --> 00:14:06,612
I call it
a laparoscopic/endoscopic hybrid surgery.

247
00:14:09,949 --> 00:14:11,417
Is that really possible?

248
00:14:13,018 --> 00:14:15,120
If successful, we can present it
at the next conference.

249
00:14:15,187 --> 00:14:19,391
Really? That means this hospital's fame
will rise even more.

250
00:14:21,594 --> 00:14:22,928
Please let me do it.

251
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:27,600
Chief, what should we do?

252
00:14:29,168 --> 00:14:31,136
Dr. Daimon might be able to do it.

253
00:14:32,238 --> 00:14:33,772
What's with you all?

254
00:14:33,839 --> 00:14:36,609
I've never seen or heard
of such a reckless surgery!

255
00:14:36,675 --> 00:14:38,477
The patient is a dear friend of mine.

256
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:40,613
There's no way I'd trust
a freelancer of all people.

257
00:14:40,679 --> 00:14:43,682
The probability of safety
comes first in surgery.

258
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:45,684
Open surgery is the best choice.

259
00:14:47,686 --> 00:14:51,757
Well, it's as Dr. Kaji says.

260
00:14:52,391 --> 00:14:53,225
Certainly.

261
00:14:53,292 --> 00:14:55,160
- Ah, certainly.
- Certainly.

262
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:57,463
- Certainly.
- Certainly.

263
00:15:13,846 --> 00:15:17,249
We decided to go with
an open abdominal surgery after all.

264
00:15:18,651 --> 00:15:21,553
You're kidding, right?
How long until I can leave?

265
00:15:21,620 --> 00:15:24,790
- Two weeks.
- No way! That won't work for me!

266
00:15:24,857 --> 00:15:27,326
I came here because you said
you could do a laparoscopy.

267
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:30,462
Patients should listen to their doctor.

268
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:34,266
Between 7:00 a.m. Saturday
and 8:00 a.m. Monday.

269
00:15:34,566 --> 00:15:38,170
Get everything done in those 49 hours
and get me back to work.

270
00:15:38,637 --> 00:15:41,740
In 49 hours? You know that's impossible.

271
00:15:42,041 --> 00:15:43,309
Why 49 hours anyways?

272
00:15:43,375 --> 00:15:45,177
That 49 hours is the only time

273
00:15:45,244 --> 00:15:48,013
the major markets of London,
New York and Tokyo stop trading.

274
00:15:49,214 --> 00:15:51,183
- That's crazy.
- You can't do it?

275
00:15:52,618 --> 00:15:53,686
It's impossible.

276
00:15:55,287 --> 00:15:56,755
Then I'll go to another hospital.

277
00:15:58,991 --> 00:16:02,227
- What's this about leaving the hospital?
- Wait a minute!

278
00:16:02,428 --> 00:16:05,064
Getting everything done
in 49 hours is impossible anywhere.

279
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:06,899
I'll find a doctor to do a laparoscopy.

280
00:16:07,066 --> 00:16:08,434
I said that'd be dangerous!

281
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:11,437
That's what a super doctor is for.
You're not one at all.

282
00:16:11,503 --> 00:16:13,205
That's right, Mr. Yotsuya.

283
00:16:13,706 --> 00:16:14,974
Who the hell are you!

284
00:16:16,141 --> 00:16:18,143
Laparoscopic surgery is the best.

285
00:16:18,510 --> 00:16:21,880
You can easily get out of here
within 49 hours after that.

286
00:16:22,247 --> 00:16:24,483
- Is that true?
- It is.

287
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:25,751
Who are you?

288
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:27,886
I'm Daimon, a surgeon.

289
00:16:28,687 --> 00:16:30,990
- Doctor, can you do it?
- Yes, of course.

290
00:16:31,256 --> 00:16:32,691
If it's me, I can do it.

291
00:16:32,758 --> 00:16:34,259
SONOKA CHIBA
CHIEF NURSE

292
00:16:35,427 --> 00:16:37,830
Yotsuya, she isn't one of our doctors.

293
00:16:37,896 --> 00:16:40,032
She's a contracted freelance doctor.

294
00:16:40,099 --> 00:16:41,633
Her experience is shady,
don't believe her!

295
00:16:41,767 --> 00:16:44,303
If she can do it,
you can too, Kaji. Please!

296
00:16:45,070 --> 00:16:47,139
I'll never do a laparoscopy on you.

297
00:16:50,209 --> 00:16:51,477
Then she'll do it.

298
00:16:53,345 --> 00:16:55,414
Dr. Daimon, please do it.

299
00:16:56,582 --> 00:17:00,619
Please leave it to me. I will never fail.

300
00:17:11,663 --> 00:17:12,598
Professor.

301
00:17:13,866 --> 00:17:15,367
About tomorrow's operation--

302
00:17:15,434 --> 00:17:17,703
Ah, I heard,
Daimon's taking over that surgery.

303
00:17:17,770 --> 00:17:20,272
Daimon's using
the patient as a guinea pig.

304
00:17:20,439 --> 00:17:22,441
- Please stop her.
- Kaji...

305
00:17:23,008 --> 00:17:26,512
I understand your feelings,
but it's the patient's wish.

306
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:29,648
If he wants laparoscopic surgery that bad,
you know...

307
00:17:29,748 --> 00:17:32,684
That's settled, so I'd like you
to be Daimon's assistant.

308
00:17:34,153 --> 00:17:35,254
Assistant?

309
00:17:35,421 --> 00:17:37,256
Dr. Kaji, if you can attend,

310
00:17:37,389 --> 00:17:40,793
I'm sure your friend
will feel at ease, too.

311
00:17:41,493 --> 00:17:42,561
I trust you'll do it.

312
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:49,034
Dr. Kaji, wanna go for a drink?

313
00:17:49,101 --> 00:17:52,171
I got a call from a former patient
asking to come to his bar.

314
00:17:52,704 --> 00:17:54,039
I have a prior engagement.

315
00:18:05,317 --> 00:18:07,186
He's taking it quite hard.

316
00:18:07,653 --> 00:18:10,322
Can't believe they're making him
Daimon's assistant.

317
00:18:10,422 --> 00:18:11,323
What, really?

318
00:18:11,657 --> 00:18:13,192
You're kidding! His pride must be shot.

319
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:15,861
Shows that overconfident people
don't take struggles well.

320
00:18:20,532 --> 00:18:24,503
If Daimon successfully performs
the laparoscopic/endoscopic surgery,

321
00:18:24,736 --> 00:18:29,174
I can make a double presentation
along with my K-RAS research.

322
00:18:29,241 --> 00:18:32,444
That would be a big highlight
in the conference, right?

323
00:18:32,678 --> 00:18:33,512
Recently,

324
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:36,515
I was invited to a dinner meeting
with main campus professors.

325
00:18:37,216 --> 00:18:39,051
Maybe my time has finally come.

326
00:18:40,652 --> 00:18:41,520
As I thought,

327
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:45,157
you're not a person to live
in obscurity in a satellite hospital.

328
00:18:45,791 --> 00:18:47,226
Go for the department head job
at the main hospital.

329
00:18:47,292 --> 00:18:48,127
AI OKUMURA
DR. TORII'S SECRETARY

330
00:18:54,766 --> 00:18:58,203
- Dr. Kaji, do you come here often?
- No, it's my first time.

331
00:18:58,537 --> 00:19:00,105
But it's cool...

332
00:19:03,542 --> 00:19:04,510
Welcome.

333
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:09,414
That's nice.

334
00:19:12,417 --> 00:19:17,055
Dr. Kaji is divorced and single,
so he isn't worried about being seen.

335
00:19:17,122 --> 00:19:17,956
Okumura...

336
00:19:18,390 --> 00:19:20,559
Mistresses have pride, too.

337
00:19:23,362 --> 00:19:25,998
When will you divorce your wife?

338
00:19:26,064 --> 00:19:28,167
Ah, that's... um...

339
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:32,671
Ah, the next international conference
is in Paris.

340
00:19:33,338 --> 00:19:34,473
Want to come with?

341
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:37,209
Paris? Of course I do!

342
00:19:40,512 --> 00:19:44,383
Dr. Kaji, the program you did recently
was very well received.

343
00:19:44,616 --> 00:19:46,451
Really? That's good.

344
00:19:47,986 --> 00:19:50,923
Announcers like you must
get invited a lot to matchmaking dates.

345
00:19:51,056 --> 00:19:53,292
Like with IT people and fund managers.

346
00:19:53,825 --> 00:19:59,164
But the only thing those guys
have on their mind is money.

347
00:20:00,599 --> 00:20:04,436
I think it's wonderful that
you're doing surgeries no one else can do.

348
00:20:06,572 --> 00:20:07,673
Then she'll do it.

349
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:10,442
Dr. Daimon, please do it.

350
00:20:10,909 --> 00:20:12,010
Leave it to me.

351
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:18,584
Dr. Kaji? Is something wrong?

352
00:20:19,985 --> 00:20:21,620
Oh, it's nothing.

353
00:20:31,563 --> 00:20:34,066
Laparoscopy and endoscopy
at the same time?

354
00:20:34,132 --> 00:20:36,301
Don't tell me you're doing it solo.

355
00:20:36,468 --> 00:20:37,502
Yeah, I am.

356
00:20:40,539 --> 00:20:42,074
- What?
- Idiot.

357
00:20:42,374 --> 00:20:44,876
You're joking.
How many arms do you think you have?

358
00:20:44,943 --> 00:20:48,380
- There's no way you can do it.
- It's absolutely impossible!

359
00:20:48,447 --> 00:20:50,249
Yeah, even for you, Michiko,
it's impossible.

360
00:20:50,315 --> 00:20:52,317
It's okay! I have plenty of arms.

361
00:20:55,487 --> 00:20:56,622
Oh, <i>Ron!</i>

362
00:21:02,294 --> 00:21:04,196
I'm on the top!

363
00:21:04,730 --> 00:21:08,467
Come on, give me the points!
I'm on a roll today!

364
00:21:13,572 --> 00:21:16,475
Dr. Daimon, Dr. Kaji is
refusing to be the assistant.

365
00:21:16,942 --> 00:21:17,776
What?

366
00:21:23,515 --> 00:21:26,118
<i>First assistant, come to the OR right now.</i>

367
00:21:27,586 --> 00:21:29,521
- I refuse.
- Why?

368
00:21:32,424 --> 00:21:34,559
Your super doctor pride won't let you?

369
00:21:36,261 --> 00:21:38,730
Well, something like that.

370
00:21:39,197 --> 00:21:41,900
<i>Ah, you're trying to run away.</i>

371
00:21:44,436 --> 00:21:46,004
<i>We've already started anesthesia.</i>

372
00:21:46,471 --> 00:21:49,541
You're the only assistant I have.
Come to the OR right now!

373
00:21:52,277 --> 00:21:54,980
That's how you ask someone for a favor?

374
00:21:56,248 --> 00:21:58,884
Kaji, stop acting like a child.

375
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:00,285
Go assist Daimon.

376
00:22:09,661 --> 00:22:11,730
NOW IN SURGERY

377
00:22:13,699 --> 00:22:16,134
We will now begin Atsushi Yotsuya's

378
00:22:16,201 --> 00:22:17,803
endoscopic and laparoscopic...

379
00:22:17,869 --> 00:22:19,771
ENDOSCOPIC AND LAPAROSCOPIC
PARTIAL RESECTION OF THE DUODENUM

380
00:22:19,838 --> 00:22:22,507
...partial resection of the duodenum.

381
00:22:22,574 --> 00:22:23,575
Are you serious?

382
00:22:26,645 --> 00:22:30,082
BP in the 100s, heart rate in the 60s,
sinus rhythm normal.

383
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:39,224
Professor Torii told me to record
the video of this very important surgery.

384
00:22:41,059 --> 00:22:42,361
<i>- Scalpel.</i>
<i>- Yes.</i>

385
00:22:48,767 --> 00:22:50,001
- Metzen.
- Yes.

386
00:22:52,871 --> 00:22:54,840
It's finally time.

387
00:22:54,906 --> 00:22:58,643
If this succeeds, not only will
the patient maintain his quality of life,

388
00:22:58,710 --> 00:23:01,213
but medically, it'll be considered
a valuable surge--

389
00:23:01,279 --> 00:23:02,814
Hey... be quiet!

390
00:23:02,914 --> 00:23:04,049
Sorry.

391
00:23:04,683 --> 00:23:05,751
Kaneko!

392
00:23:20,932 --> 00:23:22,868
Indwelling trocar catheter inserted.

393
00:23:23,335 --> 00:23:24,703
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

394
00:23:28,907 --> 00:23:29,741
Pean.

395
00:23:46,591 --> 00:23:49,060
Elevate the head, rotate left.

396
00:23:54,166 --> 00:23:56,601
Elevate the head, rotate left. Okay.

397
00:23:56,668 --> 00:23:59,538
Now we'll detach the duodenum
from the area under the laparoscope.

398
00:24:00,772 --> 00:24:02,073
This is the critical part.

399
00:24:02,741 --> 00:24:03,809
Do the rest yourself.

400
00:24:06,011 --> 00:24:07,679
You're the primary surgeon.

401
00:24:08,747 --> 00:24:10,215
Understood.

402
00:24:10,682 --> 00:24:12,451
I'll do it myself.

403
00:24:14,786 --> 00:24:16,354
- Dissecting forceps.
- Yes.

404
00:24:27,766 --> 00:24:29,367
- This is where it starts.
- Yes.

405
00:24:29,434 --> 00:24:33,638
This is the laparoscopic/endoscopic hybrid
that even Dr. Kaji couldn't do.

406
00:24:33,705 --> 00:24:37,476
How on earth is she going to do it alone?
The "Daimon Technique."

407
00:24:38,243 --> 00:24:40,512
Oh, I named it on my own just now.

408
00:24:41,246 --> 00:24:42,280
Pretty cool!

409
00:24:55,026 --> 00:24:56,328
- Yes.
- Yes.

410
00:25:22,153 --> 00:25:23,755
Dr. Daimon, what's wrong?

411
00:25:27,626 --> 00:25:28,527
Huh?

412
00:25:37,536 --> 00:25:39,471
- I can't do it.
- Huh?

413
00:25:39,538 --> 00:25:40,939
- What?
- You can't do it?

414
00:25:41,006 --> 00:25:42,173
Huh?

415
00:25:44,242 --> 00:25:45,744
I thought I could do it,

416
00:25:47,612 --> 00:25:48,980
but this is impossible!

417
00:25:50,549 --> 00:25:52,183
It's too late to say that!

418
00:25:59,958 --> 00:26:00,792
Hey!

419
00:26:01,793 --> 00:26:03,895
Oh, my. It's impossible like you said.

420
00:26:03,962 --> 00:26:06,264
- What'd she say?
- She's kidding, right?

421
00:26:07,465 --> 00:26:08,400
I'm sorry!

422
00:26:10,735 --> 00:26:11,670
Idiot!

423
00:26:13,071 --> 00:26:15,707
How can you as a surgeon
give up during a surgery?

424
00:26:17,509 --> 00:26:19,844
Idiot! If you can't do it,
say so before you begin!

425
00:26:19,911 --> 00:26:20,745
Daimon!

426
00:26:22,180 --> 00:26:23,548
Dr. Kaji, please.

427
00:26:24,249 --> 00:26:25,550
Please help me.

428
00:26:30,622 --> 00:26:31,456
Please!

429
00:26:36,962 --> 00:26:37,796
Move.

430
00:26:38,930 --> 00:26:40,298
I'll work the laparoscope.

431
00:26:40,365 --> 00:26:42,734
- You mark the spot with the endoscope.
- Yes.

432
00:26:45,537 --> 00:26:47,439
You too. Put the camera down
and give me a hand!

433
00:26:48,106 --> 00:26:48,940
Yes!

434
00:26:49,007 --> 00:26:51,643
- Vitals.
- BP 100, heart rate 60, holding steady.

435
00:26:52,444 --> 00:26:53,912
With the endoscope,
5 millimeters from the lesion...

436
00:26:53,979 --> 00:26:55,180
ENDOSCOPE
LAPAROSCOPE

437
00:26:55,246 --> 00:26:57,048
... puncture with a pointed scalpel
and coagulate.

438
00:26:57,115 --> 00:27:00,518
So the resected part can be seen from
the laparoscope, marking will be done.

439
00:27:00,852 --> 00:27:02,988
- Dissection forceps. Tweezer.
- Yes.

440
00:27:03,054 --> 00:27:04,422
Please give me the tweezer.

441
00:27:04,489 --> 00:27:07,459
Seriously, what's gonna happen?
What about the hybrid surgery?

442
00:27:07,525 --> 00:27:09,127
The Daimon Technique?

443
00:27:18,069 --> 00:27:20,138
I'll follow the marks and resect.

444
00:27:21,406 --> 00:27:23,608
- Tell me the position.
- Okay.

445
00:27:25,010 --> 00:27:26,144
Down 5 millimeters.

446
00:27:28,913 --> 00:27:29,748
Okay.

447
00:27:33,618 --> 00:27:35,286
Continue right 5 millimeters.

448
00:27:38,456 --> 00:27:39,290
Okay.

449
00:27:40,859 --> 00:27:42,861
Another 5 millimeters to the right.

450
00:27:44,963 --> 00:27:45,797
Okay.

451
00:27:57,342 --> 00:27:58,343
Up 3 millimeters.

452
00:27:59,744 --> 00:28:00,578
Okay.

453
00:28:03,448 --> 00:28:04,683
Up 3 millimeters.

454
00:28:06,718 --> 00:28:07,719
Okay.

455
00:28:07,786 --> 00:28:09,454
This is just a joint operation.

456
00:28:09,888 --> 00:28:11,723
I can't present this at the conference!

457
00:28:12,924 --> 00:28:15,326
Oh, Professor? Professor!

458
00:28:15,560 --> 00:28:18,029
Professor...

459
00:28:19,364 --> 00:28:20,632
- Extraction bag.
- Yes.

460
00:28:20,699 --> 00:28:21,533
EXTRACTION BAG

461
00:28:29,174 --> 00:28:30,508
- Can you see it?
- Yes.

462
00:28:36,047 --> 00:28:36,915
It's in.

463
00:28:45,223 --> 00:28:46,191
Suture is done.

464
00:28:51,763 --> 00:28:52,630
Yes?

465
00:28:54,165 --> 00:28:55,133
Nothing.

466
00:28:55,900 --> 00:28:58,136
Ah, what's the time?

467
00:28:58,737 --> 00:29:02,373
Surgery ended at 11:31.
Anesthesia around 12:00.

468
00:29:02,974 --> 00:29:05,143
He should be fully awake by evening.

469
00:29:07,378 --> 00:29:08,213
Okay.

470
00:29:09,214 --> 00:29:12,650
At this rate, Yotsuya's request
will be met with time to spare.

471
00:29:12,717 --> 00:29:14,853
Thanks for your hard work, everyone.

472
00:29:17,522 --> 00:29:18,656
Dr. Kaji.

473
00:29:18,723 --> 00:29:22,660
It was an honor to observe
your laparoscopic surgery this closely.

474
00:29:22,727 --> 00:29:25,063
I learned a lot. Thank you very much.

475
00:29:28,366 --> 00:29:29,200
You.

476
00:29:29,367 --> 00:29:32,470
- Did you plan from the begin--
- I learned a lot, too.

477
00:29:33,438 --> 00:29:37,275
Dr. Kaji, if you weren't there,
I don't know what I would've done.

478
00:29:37,709 --> 00:29:40,812
No kidding! I didn't know
what would happen for a while there.

479
00:29:41,980 --> 00:29:44,649
I'm really sorry an inexperienced doctor
like me got smart with you

480
00:29:44,749 --> 00:29:48,086
without knowing how good
your divine hands really are.

481
00:29:51,322 --> 00:29:52,157
Well...

482
00:29:53,525 --> 00:29:54,826
it's fine if you get that.

483
00:29:56,027 --> 00:29:58,530
Dr. Daimon,
Professor Torii is calling you.

484
00:30:03,301 --> 00:30:05,837
What's the meaning of this
after all that big talk?

485
00:30:06,805 --> 00:30:11,409
Seriously. I've never heard of or seen
a surgeon quit in the middle of surgery.

486
00:30:12,510 --> 00:30:16,114
You're just a freelancer.
How irresponsible.

487
00:30:18,383 --> 00:30:21,886
Well, it's a good thing
it didn't become a big problem, yes?

488
00:30:22,053 --> 00:30:25,990
Well, even though an open surgery
was the best choice, of course.

489
00:30:26,391 --> 00:30:29,494
It all worked out thanks to you, Dr. Kaji.

490
00:30:29,561 --> 00:30:32,630
Don't you have anything to say?
Are you even feeling remorse?

491
00:30:37,702 --> 00:30:39,971
I deeply apologize.

492
00:30:46,578 --> 00:30:48,046
Thanks, Kaji.

493
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:51,883
If it wasn't for your experience,
who knows what would've happened.

494
00:30:52,250 --> 00:30:54,018
Seriously, I'm disappointed in Daimon.

495
00:30:54,385 --> 00:30:58,489
She appealed for a reckless surgery,
convinced the patient and then failed.

496
00:31:01,192 --> 00:31:03,695
She... didn't fail.

497
00:31:03,761 --> 00:31:05,029
Huh?

498
00:31:07,131 --> 00:31:08,233
Excuse me.

499
00:31:23,815 --> 00:31:27,085
Sorry for making you work
on your day off again.

500
00:31:27,518 --> 00:31:29,320
Is your daughter okay?

501
00:31:30,021 --> 00:31:31,923
My ex is taking care of her.

502
00:31:32,390 --> 00:31:33,258
I see.

503
00:31:35,760 --> 00:31:39,330
My daughter's doing "The White Hare
of Inaba" for the next parents' day.

504
00:31:41,266 --> 00:31:42,834
Do you remember the story?

505
00:31:43,902 --> 00:31:49,140
Let's see. As I recall,
there was a hare and a shark.

506
00:31:50,141 --> 00:31:54,078
The white hare wanted to cross the water
to the other shore, and said to the shark,

507
00:31:54,245 --> 00:31:57,949
"Mr. Shark, let's compare
who has a bigger family, you or me."

508
00:31:58,016 --> 00:31:59,217
Ah, I remember.

509
00:31:59,384 --> 00:32:01,185
The sharks line up in a row

510
00:32:01,452 --> 00:32:04,088
<i>and the hare jumps across their backs.</i>

511
00:32:04,555 --> 00:32:08,860
But when the white hare was almost there,
he was so happy, and he said,

512
00:32:09,327 --> 00:32:11,029
"You guys were fooled."

513
00:32:13,564 --> 00:32:14,933
The angry shark

514
00:32:15,333 --> 00:32:18,102
ripped all the hair off of the white hare,

515
00:32:18,303 --> 00:32:20,838
and before he knew it, he was all naked.

516
00:32:24,375 --> 00:32:26,911
You be careful, too.
Thanks for your hard work.

517
00:32:29,981 --> 00:32:31,282
Thanks for your hard work.

518
00:32:53,771 --> 00:32:55,974
- I want you to come with me. Just come.
- Why?

519
00:32:56,140 --> 00:32:58,042
W-- wait!

520
00:33:05,850 --> 00:33:08,686
Dr. Daimon and Dr. Kaji?

521
00:33:14,425 --> 00:33:15,293
What?

522
00:33:24,602 --> 00:33:26,170
What is this?

523
00:33:28,139 --> 00:33:29,140
Just something...

524
00:33:29,207 --> 00:33:32,844
I told you before that I won't do anything
that doesn't require a medical license.

525
00:33:32,944 --> 00:33:34,045
Like going for a drive,

526
00:33:34,112 --> 00:33:37,448
going on a worthless walk
at a romantic place, et cetera.

527
00:33:37,515 --> 00:33:40,184
I know. It's something
I can't talk about at the hospital.

528
00:33:40,651 --> 00:33:41,519
Huh?

529
00:33:43,521 --> 00:33:46,457
Today's operation
went exactly as you planned.

530
00:33:48,760 --> 00:33:50,028
You knew from the start,

531
00:33:50,128 --> 00:33:54,065
it was impossible to do laparoscopy
and endoscopy together on your own, right?

532
00:33:54,298 --> 00:33:55,500
What are you saying?

533
00:33:55,967 --> 00:33:58,269
All I did was cut
according to the endoscopy marks.

534
00:33:59,837 --> 00:34:04,542
You made it look like I was in charge,
but actually, you took advantage of me.

535
00:34:04,809 --> 00:34:06,277
You're reading too much into it.

536
00:34:07,111 --> 00:34:08,246
Don't take me for a fool!

537
00:34:09,280 --> 00:34:11,783
You can fool others,
but you can't fool me.

538
00:34:12,316 --> 00:34:13,518
Why'd you do it?

539
00:34:14,285 --> 00:34:16,187
- Tell me!
- Then you tell me.

540
00:34:16,421 --> 00:34:19,957
If I had asked you from the start
to help me with my surgery,

541
00:34:20,024 --> 00:34:22,026
would you have agreed to it?

542
00:34:22,593 --> 00:34:23,461
Don't joke!

543
00:34:25,997 --> 00:34:29,067
You set it up
so I'd have to help you on site, right?

544
00:34:30,001 --> 00:34:32,570
Then why did you make me
look good in front of everyone?

545
00:34:33,738 --> 00:34:35,740
There's nothing in it for you, so why?

546
00:34:39,010 --> 00:34:41,345
Why are doctors like this?

547
00:34:42,246 --> 00:34:44,882
Especially doctors
at university hospitals.

548
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:45,917
What'd you say?

549
00:34:46,384 --> 00:34:49,921
Pride and honor doesn't even amount
to ten yen. I can't believe it.

550
00:34:49,987 --> 00:34:53,791
Doctors who put themselves in critical
places without payback are unbelievable.

551
00:34:53,858 --> 00:34:56,094
- Is that so?
- No way.

552
00:34:56,861 --> 00:34:58,463
No doctors like that exist.

553
00:34:59,397 --> 00:35:01,165
There's one right there.

554
00:35:01,666 --> 00:35:05,169
To me, surgery is priceless life work.

555
00:35:09,640 --> 00:35:12,376
Who am I kidding...

556
00:35:13,344 --> 00:35:15,947
- Are you mocking me?
- No.

557
00:35:16,781 --> 00:35:19,717
Your laparoscopic surgery was brilliant.

558
00:35:21,552 --> 00:35:25,456
Getting to watch your surgery
was payback for me.

559
00:35:29,327 --> 00:35:33,631
Well, your endoscopy was quite good, too.

560
00:35:34,098 --> 00:35:34,932
Well, thanks.

561
00:35:36,200 --> 00:35:39,570
Then how about a drink to celebrate
the success? With champagne or something.

562
00:35:39,670 --> 00:35:41,105
- No, thanks.
- It's okay!

563
00:35:41,239 --> 00:35:44,208
Morimoto will let me know.
Plus I'll leave the car.

564
00:35:44,342 --> 00:35:46,677
I said I won't do it, so I won't do it.

565
00:35:49,647 --> 00:35:53,117
Damn her! The nerve of a freelancer!

566
00:36:02,760 --> 00:36:08,199
<i>From now, Professor Busujima will make</i>
<i>the Chief's rounds of the surgery ward.</i>

567
00:36:17,508 --> 00:36:18,609
So,

568
00:36:18,876 --> 00:36:23,447
what happened to the surgery you wanted
to present at the academic conference?

569
00:36:23,814 --> 00:36:25,249
It was a success, but...

570
00:36:25,416 --> 00:36:26,851
Is there a problem?

571
00:36:27,251 --> 00:36:29,320
That was just Daimon saying things.

572
00:36:29,820 --> 00:36:31,822
- Oh?
- Indeed.

573
00:36:32,523 --> 00:36:35,226
If Kaji didn't take her place,
who knows what would've happened.

574
00:36:35,293 --> 00:36:36,327
Is that so.

575
00:36:39,096 --> 00:36:41,799
Dr. Kaji, thank you.

576
00:36:44,602 --> 00:36:47,104
You're definitely the ace of #2 Surgery.

577
00:36:48,806 --> 00:36:50,007
That was a great comeback.

578
00:37:08,426 --> 00:37:10,294
Akira? What's wrong?

579
00:37:10,361 --> 00:37:12,029
Just making a courtesy call.

580
00:37:13,564 --> 00:37:17,134
The duodenal cancer surgery
Daimon performed...

581
00:37:17,201 --> 00:37:18,336
A melon for you.

582
00:37:19,503 --> 00:37:23,975
Naturally, we will charge you overtime
and a special allowance.

583
00:37:24,709 --> 00:37:25,743
Here's the bill.

584
00:37:28,112 --> 00:37:29,313
468,000 YEN - FOR WORKING
ON A DAY OFF AND SPECIAL ALLOWANCE

585
00:37:29,380 --> 00:37:32,216
Special allowance?
I can't approve such a thing.

586
00:37:32,683 --> 00:37:35,353
Wasn't she supposed to do
that surgery by herself?

587
00:37:35,419 --> 00:37:36,554
- Certainly.
- Certainly.

588
00:37:37,555 --> 00:37:41,926
She did get help from her assistant,
but the primary surgeon was Daimon.

589
00:37:44,128 --> 00:37:47,932
I'm glad to hear
that the patient was pleased as well.

590
00:38:01,045 --> 00:38:03,281
I'm happy you can go home so soon.

591
00:38:03,848 --> 00:38:05,650
Remember not to overexert yourself.

592
00:38:06,217 --> 00:38:07,385
You're the best!

593
00:38:07,451 --> 00:38:10,855
Thanks to you, I'm able to get back
to work in 49 hours. Thank you.

594
00:38:11,489 --> 00:38:13,524
The cancer was completely removed.

595
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:15,726
You're really a super doctor.

596
00:38:16,127 --> 00:38:16,961
Yotsuya...

597
00:38:18,329 --> 00:38:19,297
I'm in debt to you.

598
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:22,500
I just did what a surgeon should do.

599
00:38:23,167 --> 00:38:27,071
From now on, don't just think about money,
think of your health as well.

600
00:38:29,573 --> 00:38:32,510
I'm sorry, but I have
a demonstration surgery in Kyoto.

601
00:38:33,311 --> 00:38:35,746
Morimoto's taking over,
so I leave the rest to you.

602
00:38:36,047 --> 00:38:36,881
Yes.

603
00:38:37,281 --> 00:38:38,115
Excuse me.

604
00:38:39,617 --> 00:38:40,451
Well then.

605
00:38:51,762 --> 00:38:52,697
What is it?

606
00:38:54,265 --> 00:38:57,435
You know... that thing.

607
00:38:58,369 --> 00:39:01,472
That thing you tried
to give me before surgery.

608
00:39:02,106 --> 00:39:03,974
Oh, if you mean the tip,
I already gave it.

609
00:39:04,742 --> 00:39:05,609
Already gave it?

610
00:39:05,676 --> 00:39:08,179
The manager came by
for a courtesy call with a melon.

611
00:39:08,579 --> 00:39:11,816
- Whose manager?
- The primary surgeon's manager.

612
00:39:12,416 --> 00:39:13,551
What?

613
00:39:20,224 --> 00:39:21,892
Wait, wait a minute!

614
00:39:22,560 --> 00:39:25,029
This is Dr. Kaji, the Super Doctor!

615
00:39:25,329 --> 00:39:27,098
I understand you're helping Daimon.

616
00:39:28,799 --> 00:39:30,868
- Give me the money.
- What?

617
00:39:31,335 --> 00:39:34,238
The tip from Yotsuya! I did the surgery.

618
00:39:34,305 --> 00:39:36,674
Speaking of money, Dr. Kaji,

619
00:39:37,074 --> 00:39:40,478
I was extremely moved
when I saw you on TV the other day!

620
00:39:42,680 --> 00:39:44,148
"It's not about money.

621
00:39:44,615 --> 00:39:48,986
To me, surgery is priceless life work."

622
00:39:49,286 --> 00:39:54,558
That comment was so touching,
I was overcome with emotion!

623
00:40:05,035 --> 00:40:08,439
Now then. What did you want from me?

624
00:40:09,206 --> 00:40:10,174
Never mind!

625
00:40:20,618 --> 00:40:23,888
- Ah, that felt so good!
- Ah, that was heaven!

626
00:40:26,690 --> 00:40:27,525
Yes.

627
00:40:35,566 --> 00:40:37,668
Wow!

628
00:40:38,135 --> 00:40:41,272
Michiko, you really wanted to do
that surgery, huh?

629
00:40:42,273 --> 00:40:43,107
I guess.

630
00:40:43,207 --> 00:40:46,076
So how was it?
Dr. Kaji's laparoscopic surgery.

631
00:40:46,577 --> 00:40:48,746
The image of
the super doctor's divine hands,

632
00:40:48,813 --> 00:40:52,783
I burned it into my mind,
so I think I can do a good job next time.

633
00:40:53,150 --> 00:40:55,519
What'll you do with that surgical skill?

634
00:40:55,586 --> 00:40:59,323
You'd have less debt if you directed
your passion towards money.

635
00:40:59,390 --> 00:41:00,891
You're right.

636
00:41:01,358 --> 00:41:03,260
Kaji was the primary surgeon,

637
00:41:03,427 --> 00:41:06,397
and they wouldn't pay you the special
off-day surgery allowance either.

638
00:41:08,199 --> 00:41:09,500
What about the gratuity?

639
00:41:09,700 --> 00:41:12,503
Nope, that went to Kaji as well.

640
00:41:13,037 --> 00:41:15,806
What the heck, I missed out again.

641
00:41:17,241 --> 00:41:18,776
Akira, lend me some money.

642
00:41:19,276 --> 00:41:21,712
- No.
- Why not? Give it to me. Okay?

643
00:41:22,580 --> 00:41:24,582
Hey. What are you doing?

644
00:41:24,882 --> 00:41:27,284
- Stop it!
- Just a little!

645
00:41:27,818 --> 00:41:30,087
<i>She hates groups, she hates authority,</i>

646
00:41:30,154 --> 00:41:31,655
<i>and she hates restraints.</i>

647
00:41:32,456 --> 00:41:36,594
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill to work her way up.</i>

648
00:41:50,040 --> 00:41:52,610
So your payback was money after all.

649
00:41:53,210 --> 00:41:54,879
Huh? I don't know what you mean.

650
00:41:55,312 --> 00:41:57,014
- Cut the crap, Demon.
- It's Daimon.

651
00:41:57,081 --> 00:41:58,148
- Demon.
- Daimon.

652
00:41:58,215 --> 00:41:59,517
- Demon!
- It's Michiko Daimon.

653
00:41:59,583 --> 00:42:01,819
Isn't something off with both of them?

654
00:42:02,486 --> 00:42:03,387
Really, huh?

655
00:42:16,300 --> 00:42:18,502
- All right, we'll start.
- Thank you.

656
00:42:19,737 --> 00:42:22,640
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

657
00:42:23,807 --> 00:42:25,009
<i>Also known as...</i>

658
00:42:26,210 --> 00:42:27,545
<i>Doctor X.</i>

659
00:42:30,814 --> 00:42:35,486
Welcome to my ramshackle home.
Please make yourself comfortable.

660
00:42:42,993 --> 00:42:47,898
Chief Busujima, did Daimon mess up again?

661
00:42:50,034 --> 00:42:53,737
I have one thing I'd like to hear.

662
00:42:54,905 --> 00:42:55,739
What is it?

663
00:42:59,043 --> 00:43:03,080
Do you know the person known as Doctor X?

664
00:43:05,916 --> 00:43:09,787
The person who's pulled off
many miraculous surgeries,

665
00:43:10,321 --> 00:43:12,122
Doctor X.

666
00:43:15,326 --> 00:43:17,061
Doctor X?

667
00:43:19,396 --> 00:43:21,298
They've collected a lot of debt,

668
00:43:22,199 --> 00:43:26,537
and have done
a lot of shady operations for money.

669
00:43:32,710 --> 00:43:35,245
You know her well, right?

670
00:45:19,450 --> 00:45:20,551
This drama is fiction. All names of people
and organizations are fictional.

671
00:45:20,617 --> 00:45:21,752
Medical practices in the drama vary
depending on a person's medical condition.

672
00:45:21,819 --> 00:45:22,820
Subtitle translation by Paul Koehler

673
00:45:22,886 --> 00:45:23,721
NEXT EPISODE

674
00:45:23,787 --> 00:45:25,189
It's dangerous if I don't take that!

675
00:45:25,255 --> 00:45:26,090
<i>Who are you?</i>

676
00:45:26,156 --> 00:45:27,024
IS THE ONE LYING THE PATIENT, OR...

677
00:45:27,091 --> 00:45:27,991
<i>That child isn't lying!</i>

678
00:45:28,058 --> 00:45:29,026
Didn't you mess up the operation?

679
00:45:29,093 --> 00:45:29,927
THE DOCTOR?

680
00:45:29,993 --> 00:45:32,429
<i>- Medical miss.</i>
<i>- If we don't hurry and operate...</i>

681
00:45:32,496 --> 00:45:35,499
<i>- The hospital won't take responsibility?</i>
<i>- I won't forgive that!</i>

682
00:45:35,899 --> 00:45:37,801
<i>I will not fail.</i>
